Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Integrate parametric SSI into full boolean pipeline with
 JSON comparison

Step 2: Full pipeline integration.

New: integrate_parametric.rs (327 lines)
- create_loops_stores_parametric(): replaces mesh extract_interference with
  parametric_intersection_curves() for each face pair
- estimate_surface_bounds(): infers UV bounds from face vertex projections
  (no BoundedSurface trait requirement)
- process_one_pair_parametric(): full shell-pair processing pipeline
- and_parametric(), or_parametric(), subtract_parametric(): public API

Changes to existing code:
- loops_store/mod.rs: made 6 methods pub(crate) for reuse
- boolean_comparison.rs: now runs BOTH mesh and parametric paths,
  outputs JSON comparison showing topology/bbox differences

Test results (comparison):
| Test                     | Mesh faces | Parametric faces | Notes           |
|--------------------------|-----------|-----------------|-----------------|
| cube_cube_and            | 6         | 0               | plane-plane SSI pending |
| cube_cube_or             | 12        | 0               | plane-plane SSI pending |
| cube_cube_subtract       | 9         | 0               | plane-plane SSI pending |
| cube_cylinder_subtract   | 9         | 0               | plane-cyl SSI pending |
| spheres_ssi              | n/a       | OK              | standalone SSI works |
| parabolas_ssi            | n/a       | 4.5e-6 error    | standalone SSI works |

Known limitation: parametric SSI Newton solver has rank-deficient Jacobian
for plane-plane intersections. Needs special-case handling for planar faces.
